.TH EL_GETS 3 "February 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
el_gets, el_line, el_insertstr, el_deletestr \- read and manipulate edited input lines
.SH LIBRARY
Editline library (libedit, \-ledit)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <histedit.h>
.PP
.BI "const char *el_gets(EditLine *el, int *count);"
.br
.BI "const LineInfo *el_line(EditLine *el);"
.br
.BI "int el_insertstr(EditLine *el, const char *str);"
.br
.BI "void el_deletestr(EditLine *el, int count);"
.br
.BI "int el_replacestr(EditLine *el, const char *str);"
.PP
.B typedef struct lineinfo {
.br
.BI "    const char *buffer;"
.br
.BI "    const char *cursor;"
.br
.BI "    const char *lastchar;"
.br
.B } LineInfo;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR el_gets ()
reads a line using the current editline mode and returns a pointer to the
internal line buffer. The returned pointer remains valid until the next
editline call that mutates the line buffer.
.PP
If
.I count
is not NULL, it receives the number of bytes in the returned line,
excluding the terminating NUL byte.
.PP
.BR el_line ()
returns a snapshot of the current line state. The fields of
.B LineInfo
reference internal storage and must not be modified.
.PP
.BR el_insertstr ()
inserts
.I str
at the cursor.
.BR el_deletestr ()
deletes up to
.I count
bytes before the cursor.
.BR el_replacestr ()
replaces the complete edited line with
.IR str .
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR el_gets ()
returns a pointer to edited line data on success.
On EOF or error it returns NULL.
.PP
.BR el_deletestr ()
does not return a value.
.BR el_insertstr ()
and
.BR el_replacestr ()
return 0 on success and \-1 on error.
.PP
.BR el_line ()
returns a non-NULL pointer on success, otherwise NULL.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid argument.
.TP
.B EINTR
Input was interrupted by a signal.
.TP
.B EILSEQ
Invalid UTF-8 sequence was encountered while UTF-8 mode is enabled.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Insufficient memory for line growth.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following program reads one line, then inserts and deletes text in it:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#include <histedit.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int
main(void)
{
    EditLine *el = el_init("prog", stdin, stdout, stderr);
    const char *line;
    int count;

    line = el_gets(el, &count);
    if (line != NULL) {
        el_insertstr(el, "prefix-");
        el_deletestr(el, 1);
        printf("got %d bytes\en", count);
    }
    el_end(el);
    return 0;
}
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR editline (3),
.BR el_init (3),
.BR el_set (3),
.BR history (3)
